# Folders: what the built-in viewer and the preview panel say about a file they cannot show: unplayable media, unreadable files and pictures, and the kinds of file named for a broken one.

## Viewer (src/files/viewer.rs)

# Said in the preview panel and viewer in place of a video or sound when the program that plays them is missing.
folders-viewer-no-ffmpeg = Folders needs ffmpeg to play videos and sounds, and it isn't installed.
# Said in the preview panel and viewer in place of a video or sound that cannot be played.
folders-viewer-unplayable = Folders can't play this. It may be damaged, or in a format ffmpeg can't play.
# What a file is called, with a or an before it, when its name says it is that kind but its bytes are not, such as a cut-short one; shown in the viewer and preview panel: PDF document.
folders-viewer-kind-pdf = a PDF document
# What a file is called, with a or an before it, when its name says it is that kind but its bytes are not, such as a cut-short one; shown in the viewer and preview panel: PNG picture.
folders-viewer-kind-png = a PNG picture
